          "**Phases of growth (Karlberg)**: the **infancy phase** is nutrition-driven and decelerating, the **childhood phase** from about 1 year is driven by **growth hormone and IGF-1**, and the **pubertal phase** by sex steroids plus GH - faltering in infancy is almost always nutritional. [Nelson 22e]",
