      "Acute diarrhoea is **3 or more loose or watery stools in 24 hours**; children die of **water and salt loss**, so management is to classify dehydration by **two of four signs**, replace fluid by **Plan A, B or C** with **low-osmolarity ORS** (or Ringer lactate), give **zinc for 14 days**, keep feeding, and reserve antibiotics for **dysentery and suspected cholera** - never antimotility drugs.",
